  "_baseline_note": "Measured 2026-09-09 by fetching every URL server-side with a browser user agent, BEFORE any extractor existed. This is what a plain server fetch sees on its own, and it is the number the ladder has to beat. Three results confirm the architecture rather than contradicting it:\n  * Every large marketplace bot-walls a server fetch. amazon.com returns 200 with the title 'Amazon.com' and no metadata at all, flipkart.com returns a page titled 'Flipkart reCAPTCHA', and ajio.com returns 403 'Access Denied'. myntra.com is the exception and serves full JSON-LD with a price. This is 01-PRD.md R2 exactly, and it is why the extension is the high-fidelity path and the server fetch the fallback (03-ARCHITECTURE.md 3).\n  * youtube.com returns no usable HTML, but its oEmbed endpoint returns title, author and thumbnail. Tier 4 is not optional for video links.\n  * Open Graph carries most of the long tail: 13 of 20 URLs expose og:title with no work at all."
